{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1112510-mage-crossover-book-equivalent-of-equinox-road","id":1112510,"title":"Mage Crossover Book equivalent of Equinox Road?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-06T22:19:00-07:00","id":1112510,"title":"Mage Crossover Book equivalent of Equinox Road?","content":"Did any of the Mage: the Awakening books (either 1st or 2nd edition) delve into how Mage lore interacts with other supernaturals in the same way that Changeling: Equinox Road had a chapter devoted to how Changelings interacted with Mages, Vampires, Prometheans, and Hunters?<br /> <br /> Obviously, Equinox Road already covered hot Mage-on-Changeling action, but I was curious about mages interacting with the other groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12390,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12390-gadren","user":"gadren","date":". 07-07-2017, 01:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12390-gadren","name":"gadren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T22:26:48-07:00","id":1112514,"title":"","content":"Tome of the Mysteries had sections on the limitations of (non-Imperial) sorcery and their interactions as regards the other gamelines. Of course, at the time the book came out, &quot;the other gamelines&quot; only covered Vampire, Werewolf, and Promethean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T22:46:32-07:00","id":1112516,"title":"","content":"All of the 1E Order books (except maybe Free Council) have a section on how they interact with other supernaturals, but they're heavy on that nWoD crossover thing where it doesn't actually say anything more substantive than &quot;sometimes they hang out, but it's a very bad idea and you shouldn't do it.&quot; I think most of the mechanical side of Mage crossover happens in other gameline books. Like the Promethean book Pandora's Book has rules for Mages interacting with Flux.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T08:44:37-07:00","id":1112706,"title":"","content":"Chronicles of Darkness is consistently vague in detailing with finality how various supernaturals interact with each other. What would Mage Sight show during the performance of a Cruac ritual? How would Death Arcana work with Geists? The repliers above gave some excellent sources. Go read up Dark Eras - you've got Awakened chasing Mysteries in the same time and place as pre-Forsaken Uratha, in Companions, sorcerers and Arisen operate in the Mutapan Empire. And so far, Dark Eras 2 will include mages and Deviants in the age of Galileio. <br /> <br /> In fact, every chapter has a section concerning what other supernaturals might be up to during the given era. The rest is up to imagination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T09:03:14-07:00","id":1112717,"title":"","content":"Well, in 2E a geist is just a ghost with a certain Manifestation so Death would affect it the same way it would affect any other ghosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T09:47:21-07:00","id":1112748,"title":"","content":"And 1e Geist was quite clear that mechanically it required both Death and Spirit to affect a Geist. (Although the in-character reason was variable)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}